# TOY & JOY Phase 1 — System-Wide Confidence Test Pass

Run date: 2026-08-10 (Africa/Cairo)

Environment: local Laravel application, PHP 8.4.21, Laravel 13.24.0, MariaDB/XAMPP on 127.0.0.1:3306, disposable named schemas only. No production data, SQLite, commit, or push was used.

## Executive verdict

**SYSTEM CONFIDENCE: LOW**

There is substantial passing local/dev evidence across customer, party, rental asset, returns, gift card, reporting, money-calculation, and selected MariaDB concurrency paths. The system is not yet system-wide high-confidence because the current run could not establish the critical POS checkout/race path with a valid shift fixture, authenticated browser confidence was blocked before reaching business screens, offline workflows are not implemented, several documented capabilities remain partial, and a current full regression could not complete.

No new valid critical product defect was proven by this pass. The non-passing current test records were classified as fixture, test-infrastructure, or environment blockers unless the application behavior itself was reached and contradicted a requirement.

